<phyphox version="1.14" locale="en">
  <title>Floor Tile Tap Test</title>
  <category>Data centre</category>
  <icon>TAP</icon>
  <description>
        WHAT IT DOES
        Finds loose, cracked and unsupported raised floor tiles by the note they make when you tap them. A raised floor is floor panels held up on short legs, with a gap underneath for cables and cool air.

        HOW
        A tile sitting properly on four pedestals rings high and dies away quickly. Pedestals are the short legs a tile sits on. Take a pedestal away, crack the tile, or leave a stringer loose, and it rings lower and rumbles on. A stringer is one of the metal rails that link the legs. It is exactly why a cracked mug sounds dull compared with a good one.

        Engineers have tapped things and listened for a hundred years. This just puts a number on what your ear already notices. So you can compare a hundred tiles without trusting your memory of the first one.

        WHY YOU CARE
        Loose tiles trip people. They leak air out of the underfloor plenum, the open space beneath the tiles that carries cool air. They are also a sign the grid, the metal frame that holds the tiles, is going. The usual way to find them is to walk on every one and hope you notice.

        HOW TO RUN IT
        1. Find a tile you KNOW is solid. Tap it, then press Set this tile as the reference. The reference is the known-good tile you score the rest against.
        2. Walk the room. Tap each tile, press Log this tile.
        3. Press Next tile to advance the number so your log matches the floor plan.
        4. Anything ringing well below the reference is worth lifting.

        THE ONE THING THAT MATTERS
        Tap the same way every single time. Middle of the tile, same knuckle or same screwdriver handle, same force. Consistency beats technique - a sloppy tap repeated identically is more useful than a perfect tap done differently each time.

        Do not tap over a pedestal. Every tile sounds dead there, good or bad, and you will learn nothing.

        SAFETY
        This finds candidates. It is not permission to open the floor. Check what is standing on a tile and what runs underneath it before lifting anything.
    </description>

  <data-containers>
    <container size="16384">recording</container>
    <container>micRate</container>
    <container>micCnt</container>
    <container>micFrom</container>
    <container size="8192">block</container>
    <container>blockN</container>

    <container size="8192">winU</container>
    <container size="8192">win</container>
    <container size="8192">windowed</container>
    <container size="8192">re</container>
    <container size="8192">im</container>
    <container>nHalf</container>
    <container>nHalf1</container>
    <container>rateHalf</container>
    <container size="4097">freq</container>
    <container size="4096">halfF</container>
    <container size="4096">halfRe</container>
    <container size="4096">halfIm</container>
    <container size="4096">mag</container>

    <container init="0">seeded</container>
    <container size="4096">peakNew</container>
    <container size="4096" init="0">peakHold</container>

    <container init="80">fLow</container>
    <container init="2000">fHigh</container>
    <container>iFrom</container>
    <container>iTo</container>
    <container size="4096">bandF</container>
    <container size="4096">bandMag</container>
    <container>ringF</container>
    <container>ringLevel</container>

    <container init="0">refF</container>
    <container init="0">hasRef</container>
    <container init="0">setRef</container>
    <container>ratio</container>
    <container>percent</container>

    <container init="1">tileId</container>
    <container>tileNext</container>
    <container init="0">logNow</container>
    <container size="0">logTile</container>
    <container size="0">logF</container>
    <container size="0">logPct</container>
    <container>logCount</container>
  </data-containers>

  <input>
    <audio append="true">
      <output>recording</output>
      <output component="rate">micRate</output>
    </audio>
  </input>

  <views>
    <view label="Tap a tile">
      <value label="The note the tile rings at" unit="Hz" size="3" precision="0">
        <input>ringF</input>
      </value>
      <separator height="0.5"/>
      <value label="Compared with the good tile" unit="%" size="2" precision="0">
        <input>percent</input>
      </value>
      <value label="Verdict">
        <input>percent</input>
        <map max="-30">MUCH lower - suspect this tile</map>
        <map max="-12">lower than the reference - worth a look</map>
        <map max="12">same as the reference</map>
        <map>higher than the reference</map>
      </value>
      <separator height="0.5"/>
      <button label="Next tile">
        <input type="value">0</input>
        <output>seeded</output>
      </button>
      <info label="Press this before every tap. It clears the previous ring so the new one is measured cleanly."/>
      <separator height="0.5"/>
      <value label="Reference set yet">
        <input>hasRef</input>
        <map max="0.5">NO - tap a good tile and set it below</map>
        <map>yes</map>
      </value>
      <value label="Reference ring" unit="Hz" precision="0">
        <input>refF</input>
      </value>
      <button label="Set this tile as the reference">
        <input type="value">1</input>
        <output>setRef</output>
      </button>
    </view>

    <view label="Log the run">
      <value label="Tile number" size="2" precision="0">
        <input>tileId</input>
      </value>
      <value label="Tiles logged" precision="0">
        <input>logCount</input>
      </value>
      <button label="Log this tile">
        <input type="value">1</input>
        <output>logNow</output>
      </button>
      <separator height="0.5"/>
      <edit label="Set the tile number" default="1" decimal="false">
        <output>tileId</output>
      </edit>
      <button label="Clear the log">
        <input type="empty"/>
        <output>logTile</output>
        <input type="empty"/>
        <output>logF</output>
        <input type="empty"/>
        <output>logPct</output>
      </button>
      <separator height="0.5"/>
      <graph label="Ring frequency by tile" labelX="Tile" labelY="Ring" unitY="Hz" style="dots" partialUpdate="true">
        <input axis="x">logTile</input>
        <input axis="y">logF</input>
      </graph>
      <info label="Walk a grid and log every tile. The outliers on this chart are the ones to lift."/>
    </view>

    <view label="Spectrum">
      <graph label="What the tap sounded like" logX="true" logY="true" labelX="Frequency" unitX="Hz" labelY="Level" unitY="a.u.">
        <input axis="x">halfF</input>
        <input axis="y">peakHold</input>
      </graph>
      <separator height="0.5"/>
      <info label="A healthy tile gives one clear peak - a pitch louder than its neighbours. Several peaks close together, or a broad smear instead of a peak, usually means the tile is moving against its stringers, the rails under it, rather than ringing. That is itself worth reporting."/>
      <separator height="0.5"/>
      <edit label="Search from" unit="Hz" default="80" decimal="false">
        <output>fLow</output>
      </edit>
      <edit label="Search to" unit="Hz" default="2000" decimal="false">
        <output>fHigh</output>
      </edit>
    </view>

    <view label="Notes">
      <info label="HOW TO TAP"/>
      <info label="Middle of the tile. Same object every time - a knuckle, or the handle of a screwdriver. Same force."/>
      <info label="Never over a pedestal - one of the short legs under the tile. There the tile cannot move, so it thuds dully whether it is perfect or broken, and every tile scores the same."/>
      <info label="Being consistent matters more than being skilful. A rough tap repeated identically a hundred times is far more useful than a perfect tap done slightly differently each time."/>
      <separator height="0.5"/>
      <info label="WHY IT COMPARES INSTEAD OF MEASURING"/>
      <info label="The actual pitch depends on the type of tile, its size, how high the floor is, and what is stacked on top. None of that is worth trying to calibrate away, and it would change in the next room anyway."/>
      <info label="So the finding is never a number on its own. The finding is: this tile rings well below its identical neighbours. That comparison survives everything above, which is why it works."/>
      <separator height="0.5"/>
      <info label="IT TELLS YOU A TILE IS DIFFERENT, NOT WHY"/>
      <info label="A lower ring means the tile is either less stiff or carrying more weight. That could be a missing pedestal, a crack, a loose stringer - or just a heavy cabinet standing on it, which is not a fault at all."/>
      <info label="Go and look. This narrows a room full of tiles down to a handful worth checking, and that is the whole job."/>
      <separator height="0.5"/>
      <info label="WHEN IT WILL NOT WORK"/>
      <info label="A data hall is loud, and the app catches the loudest thing it hears - which is not always your tap. If a reading looks obviously wrong, press Next tile and tap harder."/>
      <info label="In a really loud room this test may simply not work. That is worth knowing before you spend an hour on it."/>
      <separator height="0.5"/>
      <info label="SAFETY"/>
      <info label="Never lift a tile without checking what is standing on it and what runs underneath. This test produces a list of candidates. It is not permission to open the floor."/>
    </view>
  </views>

  <analysis sleep="0.3">
    <count>
      <input clear="false">recording</input>
      <output>micCnt</output>
    </count>
    <formula formula="max([1]-8192,0)">
      <input>micCnt</input>
      <output>micFrom</output>
    </formula>
    <subrange>
      <input as="from" clear="false">micFrom</input>
      <input as="in" clear="false">recording</input>
      <output>block</output>
    </subrange>
    <count>
      <input clear="false">block</input>
      <output clear="false">blockN</output>
    </count>

    <ramp>
      <input as="start" type="value">0</input>
      <input as="stop" type="value">1</input>
      <input as="length" clear="false">blockN</input>
      <output>winU</output>
    </ramp>
    <formula formula="0.5-0.5*cos(6.283185307179586*[1_])">
      <input>winU</input>
      <output>win</output>
    </formula>
    <multiply>
      <input as="factor">block</input>
      <input as="factor">win</input>
      <output>windowed</output>
    </multiply>
    <fft>
      <input>windowed</input>
      <output as="re">re</output>
      <output as="im">im</output>
    </fft>
    <divide>
      <input clear="false">micRate</input>
      <input type="value">2</input>
      <output>rateHalf</output>
    </divide>
    <divide>
      <input clear="false">blockN</input>
      <input type="value">2</input>
      <output clear="false">nHalf</output>
    </divide>
    <add>
      <input clear="false">nHalf</input>
      <input type="value">1</input>
      <output>nHalf1</output>
    </add>
    <ramp>
      <input as="start" type="value">0</input>
      <input as="stop">rateHalf</input>
      <input as="length" clear="false">nHalf1</input>
      <output>freq</output>
    </ramp>
    <subrange>
      <input as="from" type="value">1</input>
      <input as="to" clear="false">nHalf</input>
      <input as="in">freq</input>
      <input as="in">re</input>
      <input as="in">im</input>
      <output>halfF</output>
      <output>halfRe</output>
      <output>halfIm</output>
    </subrange>
    <formula formula="sqrt([1_]*[1_]+[2_]*[2_])">
      <input>halfRe</input>
      <input>halfIm</input>
      <output>mag</output>
    </formula>

    <formula formula="max([1_],[2_])">
      <input clear="false">peakHold</input>
      <input clear="false">mag</input>
      <output>peakNew</output>
    </formula>
    <if less="true">
      <input clear="false">seeded</input>
      <input type="value">0.5</input>
      <input clear="false">mag</input>
      <input>peakNew</input>
      <output>peakHold</output>
    </if>
    <append>
      <input type="value">1</input>
      <output>seeded</output>
    </append>

    <formula formula="max(round([1]*[2]/[3])-1,0)">
      <input clear="false">fLow</input>
      <input clear="false">blockN</input>
      <input clear="false">micRate</input>
      <output>iFrom</output>
    </formula>
    <formula formula="max(round([1]*[2]/[3])-1,1)">
      <input clear="false">fHigh</input>
      <input clear="false">blockN</input>
      <input clear="false">micRate</input>
      <output>iTo</output>
    </formula>
    <subrange>
      <input as="from" clear="false">iFrom</input>
      <input as="to" clear="false">iTo</input>
      <input as="in" clear="false">halfF</input>
      <input as="in" clear="false">peakHold</input>
      <output>bandF</output>
      <output>bandMag</output>
    </subrange>
    <max>
      <input as="x">bandF</input>
      <input as="y">bandMag</input>
      <output as="position" clear="false">ringF</output>
      <output as="max">ringLevel</output>
    </max>

    <if equal="true">
      <input clear="false">setRef</input>
      <input type="value">1</input>
      <input clear="false">ringF</input>
      <output clear="false">refF</output>
    </if>
    <if equal="true">
      <input clear="false">setRef</input>
      <input type="value">1</input>
      <input type="value">1</input>
      <output clear="false">hasRef</output>
    </if>
    <append>
      <input type="value">0</input>
      <output>setRef</output>
    </append>
    <formula formula="[1]/max([2],1)">
      <input clear="false">ringF</input>
      <input clear="false">refF</input>
      <output>ratio</output>
    </formula>
    <formula formula="100*([1]-1)">
      <input>ratio</input>
      <output clear="false">percent</output>
    </formula>

    <if equal="true">
      <input clear="false">logNow</input>
      <input type="value">1</input>
      <input clear="false">tileId</input>
      <output clear="false">logTile</output>
    </if>
    <if equal="true">
      <input clear="false">logNow</input>
      <input type="value">1</input>
      <input clear="false">ringF</input>
      <output clear="false">logF</output>
    </if>
    <if equal="true">
      <input clear="false">logNow</input>
      <input type="value">1</input>
      <input clear="false">percent</input>
      <output clear="false">logPct</output>
    </if>
    <add>
      <input clear="false">tileId</input>
      <input type="value">1</input>
      <output>tileNext</output>
    </add>
    <if equal="true">
      <input clear="false">logNow</input>
      <input type="value">1</input>
      <input>tileNext</input>
      <output clear="false">tileId</output>
    </if>
    <append>
      <input type="value">0</input>
      <output>logNow</output>
    </append>
    <count>
      <input clear="false">logTile</input>
      <output>logCount</output>
    </count>
  </analysis>

  <export>
    <set name="Tiles">
      <data name="Tile">logTile</data>
      <data name="Ring frequency (Hz)">logF</data>
      <data name="Difference from reference (%)">logPct</data>
    </set>
    <set name="Reference">
      <data name="Reference ring (Hz)">refF</data>
    </set>
    <set name="Last tap spectrum">
      <data name="Frequency (Hz)">halfF</data>
      <data name="Level (a.u.)">peakHold</data>
    </set>
  </export>
</phyphox>
